 "voiceover": "[excited, conversational] Okay, so Apple just made a touchscreen MacBook Pro, something Steve Jobs was famously against. [curious] It's the first time Touch has ever come to a Mac.\n\n[intrigued, building energy] The screen is a new tandem OLED display Apple calls PROLED XDR. It hits up to 2000 nits of brightness, with a 10,000,000:1 contrast ratio. Ars Technica says the OLED steals the show.\n\n[excited, fast] The Dynamic Island now comes to Mac too. It runs M5 Pro and M5 Max chips, with up to 24 hours of battery. [amused] Apple also showed an OLED iPad mini and an M6 iMac.\n\n[confident] If you edit photos or video, that screen is aimed right at you. According to 9to5Mac, TrendForce expects up to 1.5 million of these to ship in 2027. Pre-orders are open now, and they arrive November 6.\n\n[playful, warm] Send this to the friend who swore Apple would never make a touchscreen Mac.",
